<figure class="fig fig--paper cap-fig">
	<p class="fig-kicker">Figure · CAP theorem</p>
	<h3 class="fig-title">The network splits. Each replica must answer anyway — but with what?</h3>

	<div class="cap">
		<section class="panel is-cp" aria-labelledby="p-cp">
			<header>
				<h4 id="p-cp">Choose consistency (CP)</h4>
				<span class="chip chip-cp">refuses</span>
			</header>
			<p class="verdict">
				A replica that can't confirm it has the latest write <b>refuses the request</b>
				(or blocks until the partition heals) rather than risk answering with stale data.
			</p>
			<p class="takeaway">Every answer given is correct. Some requests get no answer at all.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="panel is-ap" aria-labelledby="p-ap">
			<header>
				<h4 id="p-ap">Choose availability (AP)</h4>
				<span class="chip chip-ap">answers</span>
			</header>
			<p class="verdict">
				Every replica <b>answers with whatever it has</b>, even if another replica,
				unreachable right now, holds a newer write.
			</p>
			<p class="takeaway">Every request gets an answer. Some answers are stale until the split heals.</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<p class="fig-note">
		<strong>Partition tolerance isn't the third option on the menu</strong> — in a real distributed system,
		the network <em>will</em> partition eventually, so P is a fact you design for, not a property you
		pick. The actual choice CAP describes is C vs A, and only <em>during</em> a partition: outside one,
		most systems give you both.
	</p>
</figure>

<style>
	.cap{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem}

	.panel{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2ddf0;border-radius:14px;padding:1rem 1.05rem 1.05rem;
		display:flex;flex-direction:column}
	.panel.is-cp{border-top:4px solid var(--accent)}
	.panel.is-ap{border-top:4px solid #c26a12}
	.panel header{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:.6rem;margin-bottom:.7rem}
	.panel h4{margin:0;font-size:.95rem;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.01em}
	.chip{font-size:.62rem;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:.22rem .55rem;border-radius:6px}
	.chip-cp{background:#edf0fb;color:var(--accent)}
	.chip-ap{background:#fbeee0;color:#a5560d}

	.verdict{font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--text)}
	.verdict b{font-weight:750}
	.takeaway{margin:0;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.7;font-weight:650;padding-top:.6rem;border-top:1px dashed #ddd6ec}
	.is-cp .takeaway{color:var(--accent-dim)}
	.is-ap .takeaway{color:#a5560d}

	@media(max-width:620px){.cap{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
